  "configuration_id": "config_044",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_006: multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, concat → acc 0.512, F1 0.477), so the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality is actually contributing useful signal or is adding noise. Config_044 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_006: it keeps the identical RNA encoder (scgpt), profile setting (multiprofile), and aggregation (avgpool), and only removes the image branch. If config_044 matches or exceeds config_006, the image is not helping and we should pivot toward RNA-centric or simpler designs; if it falls well short, the image is contributing and we should invest in optimizing fusion/aggregation. Answering this fundamental 'does multimodal help?' question before tuning fusion or aggregation is the highest-information use of the next experiment under a limited budget."
}

